messages.content:
We need to use tools. Let's search available functional groups list to know names.
{
  "tool_name": "get_available_functional_groups",
  "arguments": {}
}

We have functional groups list. Good.

Now need templates for three steps:

Step 1: Disconnection of sulfonamide: target has NS(=O)(=O) attached to aromatic ring. Sulfonamide formation forward: amine + sulfonyl chloride -> sulfonamide. So retro: break S-N bond to give sulfonyl chloride (aryl sulfonyl chloride) and aniline (the aromatic amine). So need template that breaks sulfonamide to sulfonyl chloride + amine. functional_groups_broken: sulfonamide? Actually forward forms sulfonamide, so broken groups: sulfonyl chloride (S-Cl) and amine (N-H). Formed: sulfonamide (S-N). So search.


Search templates.
{
  "tool_name": "search_template_catalog_by_criteria",
  "arguments": {
    "molecule_smiles": "Cc1ccc(NS(=O)(=O)c2ccc(/C=C/C(=O)Nc3ccccc3N)cc2)cc1",
    "functional_groups_broken": ["sulfonyl chloride", "primary amines"],
    "functional_groups_formed": ["sulfonamides"]
  }
}

We have two templates. Template ID 214705 seems appropriate: retro_smarts_template breaks sulfonamide into sulfonyl chloride (O=S(=O)-c) and aniline (NH2-aryl). Good.

Now step 2: disconnect amide bond between C(=O)N and aniline (c3ccccc3N). Use amide formation template. Search for amide formation retro (break amide to carboxylic acid and amine). Use functional_groups_broken: "carboxylic acid" and "primary amines"? Actually forward forms amide, breaking carboxylic acid and amine. So broken: aliphatic carboxylic acid? The acid is alpha,beta-unsaturated carboxylic acid (C= C - C(=O)OH). That's aliphatic carboxylic acid. So use "aliphatic carboxylic acid". And "primary amines". Formed: "amide". Search.


{
  "tool_name": "search_template_catalog_by_criteria",
  "arguments": {
    "molecule_smiles": "Cc1ccc(NS(=O)(=O)c2ccc(/C=C/C(=O)Nc3ccccc3N)cc2)cc1",
    "functional_groups_broken": ["aliphatic carboxylic acid", "primary amines"],
    "functional_groups_formed": ["amide"]
  }
}
